/** @mainpage Qore astparser Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section astparserintro astparser Module Introduction

    The \c astparser module supports reporting of %Qore-language declarations for rich language support in
    %Qore code editors.  It parses %Qore source with a
    <a href="https://tree-sitter.github.io/tree-sitter/">tree-sitter</a> grammar, which tolerates incomplete and
    erroneous code, as in a file being edited.

    This module is released under the MIT license (see \c COPYING.MIT in the source distribution for
    more information).  The module is tagged as such in the module's header (meaning it can be loaded
    unconditionally regardless of how the %Qore library was initialized).

    To use the module in a %Qore script, use the \c %%requires directive as follows:
    @code{.py} %requires astparser @endcode

    Classes provided by this module:
    - @ref astparser::AstParser "AstParser"
    - @ref astparser::AstTree "AstTree"
    - @ref astparser::AstTreeSearcher "AstTreeSearcher"

    @section astparserhighlighting Syntax Highlighting

    The tree-sitter grammar of %Qore has a highlight query (\c queries/highlights.scm), which is compiled into the
    module and installed in <tt>share/qore/treesitter/tree-sitter-qore/queries</tt> for editors that use
    tree-sitter.  @ref astparser::AstTree::getHighlights() "AstTree::getHighlights()" returns the highlighted ranges
    of a syntax tree with the capture names of the query, and the @ref qdxintro "Qdx" module uses them to highlight
    the %Qore code in the HTML documentation that doxygen generates.

    @par Example
    @code{.py}
%requires astparser

string src = "int i = 1; # one";
AstParser parser();
AstTree tree = parser.parseString(src);
foreach hash<AstHighlight> h in (tree.getHighlights()) {
    printf("%s: %y\n", h.capture, src.substr(h.start, h.end - h.start));
}
    @endcode

